{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"code","value":"function createStoreContext<TValue>(): object;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Defined in: "},{"type":"link","href":"https://github.com/TanStack/store/blob/main/packages/octane-store/src/createStoreContext.ts#L44","children":[{"type":"text","value":"octane-store/src/createStoreContext.ts:44"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Creates a typed Octane context for sharing a bundle of atoms and stores with\na subtree."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The returned "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StoreProvider"},{"type":"text","value":" only transports the provided object through\nOctane context. Consumers destructure the contextual atoms and stores, then\ncompose them with hooks like "},{"type":"link","href":"useSelector.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useSelector"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"link","href":"useAtom.md","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useAtom"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The object shape is preserved exactly, so keyed atoms and stores remain fully\ntyped when read back with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useStoreContext()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-parameters","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Parameters"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"tvalue","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"emphasis","children":[{"type":"text","value":"extends"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"object"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"returns","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"object"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"storeprovider","children":[{"type":"text","value":"StoreProvider"}]},{"type":"code","value":"StoreProvider: ComponentBody<{\n  children?: unknown;\n  value: TValue;\n}>;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"usestorecontext","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useStoreContext()"}]},{"type":"code","value":"useStoreContext: () => TValue;","lang":"ts"},{"type":"heading","depth":4,"id":"returns-2","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Returns"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TValue"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Example"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const { StoreProvider, useStoreContext } = createStoreContext<{\n  countAtom: Atom<number>\n  totalsStore: Store<{ count: number }>\n}>()\n\nfunction CountButton() @{\n  const { countAtom, totalsStore } = useStoreContext()\n  const count = useSelector(countAtom)\n  const total = useSelector(totalsStore, (state) => state.count)\n\n  <button\n    type=\"button\"\n    onClick={() =>\n      totalsStore.setState((state) => ({\n        ...state,\n        count: state.count + 1,\n      }))\n    }\n  >\n    {count + ' / ' + total}\n  </button>\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"throws","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Throws"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"When "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useStoreContext()"},{"type":"text","value":" is called outside the matching\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"StoreProvider"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-parameters","text":"Type Parameters","level":2},{"id":"tvalue","text":"TValue","level":3},{"id":"returns","text":"Returns","level":2},{"id":"storeprovider","text":"StoreProvider","level":3},{"id":"usestorecontext","text":"useStoreContext()","level":3},{"id":"returns-2","text":"Returns","level":4},{"id":"example","text":"Example","level":2},{"id":"throws","text":"Throws","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\n```ts\nfunction createStoreContext<TValue>(): object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [octane-store/src/createStoreContext.ts:44](https://github.com/TanStack/store/blob/main/packages/octane-store/src/createStoreContext.ts#L44)\n\nCreates a typed Octane context for sharing a bundle of atoms and stores with\na subtree.\n\nThe returned `StoreProvider` only transports the provided object through\nOctane context. Consumers destructure the contextual atoms and stores, then\ncompose them with hooks like [useSelector](useSelector.md) and [useAtom](useAtom.md).\n\nThe object shape is preserved exactly, so keyed atoms and stores remain fully\ntyped when read back with `useStoreContext()`.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue` *extends* `object`\n\n## Returns\n\n`object`\n\n### StoreProvider\n\n```ts\nStoreProvider: ComponentBody<{\n  children?: unknown;\n  value: TValue;\n}>;\n```\n\n### useStoreContext()\n\n```ts\nuseStoreContext: () => TValue;\n```\n\n#### Returns\n\n`TValue`\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nconst { StoreProvider, useStoreContext } = createStoreContext<{\n  countAtom: Atom<number>\n  totalsStore: Store<{ count: number }>\n}>()\n\nfunction CountButton() @{\n  const { countAtom, totalsStore } = useStoreContext()\n  const count = useSelector(countAtom)\n  const total = useSelector(totalsStore, (state) => state.count)\n\n  <button\n    type=\"button\"\n    onClick={() =>\n      totalsStore.setState((state) => ({\n        ...state,\n        count: state.count + 1,\n      }))\n    }\n  >\n    {count + ' / ' + total}\n  </button>\n}\n```\n\n## Throws\n\nWhen `useStoreContext()` is called outside the matching\n`StoreProvider`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: createStoreContext\ntitle: createStoreContext\n---\n\n```ts\nfunction createStoreContext<TValue>(): object;\n```\n\nDefined in: [octane-store/src/createStoreContext.ts:44](https://github.com/TanStack/store/blob/main/packages/octane-store/src/createStoreContext.ts#L44)\n\nCreates a typed Octane context for sharing a bundle of atoms and stores with\na subtree.\n\nThe returned `StoreProvider` only transports the provided object through\nOctane context. Consumers destructure the contextual atoms and stores, then\ncompose them with hooks like [useSelector](useSelector.md) and [useAtom](useAtom.md).\n\nThe object shape is preserved exactly, so keyed atoms and stores remain fully\ntyped when read back with `useStoreContext()`.\n\n## Type Parameters\n\n### TValue\n\n`TValue` *extends* `object`\n\n## Returns\n\n`object`\n\n### StoreProvider\n\n```ts\nStoreProvider: ComponentBody<{\n  children?: unknown;\n  value: TValue;\n}>;\n```\n\n### useStoreContext()\n\n```ts\nuseStoreContext: () => TValue;\n```\n\n#### Returns\n\n`TValue`\n\n## Example\n\n```tsx\nconst { StoreProvider, useStoreContext } = createStoreContext<{\n  countAtom: Atom<number>\n  totalsStore: Store<{ count: number }>\n}>()\n\nfunction CountButton() @{\n  const { countAtom, totalsStore } = useStoreContext()\n  const count = useSelector(countAtom)\n  const total = useSelector(totalsStore, (state) => state.count)\n\n  <button\n    type=\"button\"\n    onClick={() =>\n      totalsStore.setState((state) => ({\n        ...state,\n        count: state.count + 1,\n      }))\n    }\n  >\n    {count + ' / ' + total}\n  </button>\n}\n```\n\n## Throws\n\nWhen `useStoreContext()` is called outside the matching\n`StoreProvider`.\n"}
